The Generated JavaScript pair contract keeps each Deno TypeScript source, generated JavaScript file, generated file header, and documentation row synchronized. The Deno type-check target coverage keeps the normal type-check target list explicit and check-covered before optional Deno execution.

`Tools/check/adlaire-design-contracts.json` lists the TypeScript source inventory, generated JavaScript pairs, CSS target metadata, JSON `tokenCategories`, JSON `editorRuntimeModules`, `assetInventory`, `documentationGovernance`, Sample asset/load order, and parity terms checked against both TypeScript source and generated output. The TypeScript source inventory is synchronized with actual `TypeScript/**/*.ts` files, Deno targets, Generated JavaScript pair sources, and CSS compiler required files. The generated CSS inventory is synchronized with `TypeScript/CSS/manifest.ts`, the generated JavaScript inventory is synchronized with Generated JavaScript pairs, and the Sample asset/load order is synchronized with `Samples/design/index.html`. The Interaction audit contract keeps audit records derived one-to-one from `UI_INTERACTION_CONTRACTS`.

The JavaScript public surface contract keeps `UI/components.js`, `UI/forms.js`, `UI/content.js`, `EditorUI/editor.js`, and `EditorUI/wysiwyg.js` loadable without bundling and keeps `window.AdlaireEditor` exposed by the structured editor runtime.

The Editor runtime module registry contract keeps `Docs/Editor_Master_Spec`, JSON `editorRuntimeModules`, the flat `TypeScript/Editor/*.ts` file set, `TypeScript/Editor/index.ts`, and `EditorUI/editor.js` synchronized as the editor runtime module registry.

